 "purpose": "The terminal app: the start screen, the main menu, the active child with their settings, the safety net for errors, and the Herhalen menus.",
 "details": "App.start decides the first screen: with the lock on Stoppen (stopslot) it goes straight to that child; otherwise title screen, 'Wie ben jij?' (kinderen.kies_kind), main menu, and back to the title screen on Stoppen; Esc on the title screen exits the program. The main menu (hoofdmenu) is built from the curriculum plus fixed items in groups (Verder, Herhalen; VAKKEN with Leerstof; JIJ with avatar and shop; FEEDBACK; Stoppen). Any exception in a screen is caught by App.oeps (logged to fouten.log, the child is reassured and returns to the menu; three errors within a minute exit; LEERAVONTUUR_DEBUG=1 re-raises). Settings: the active child's settings, with start arguments overriding them for the session without being stored (voorrang). The clock window (terminal/venster.py) is started or stopped by zet_klokvenster. 'Verder' continues the last exercise stored per child, and first offers to repeat when the last one was finished and repeat questions are due.",
 "module_docstring": "De terminal-app: startscherm en hoofdmenu (de vakken komen uit het leerplan: terminal/curriculum).",
